§ `Chapters 39 and 40 -- peers, right and justice`

§§ `Chapter 39 -- the judgment of peers and the law of the land`

-- Reading taken (fork F39a): the closing words "unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by
-- the law of the land" are an exception to the whole sentence, to the passive limb (arrested ...
-- molested) as well as to the limb about the King; and "and" is read as "and": both are needed.
-- The two facts the exception names are taken as plain inputs.
-- src:85 | No freeman shall be arrested, or detained in prison, or deprived of his freehold, or outlawed, or banished, or in any way molested;
-- src:85 | and we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land.
@ref Chapter 39 clause 39.1-39.2 (src:85)
GIVEN `the person is a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` IS
    IF `the person is a freeman`
    THEN IF   `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers`
          AND `it is done by the law of the land`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land".
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: unless because "unless" names the judgment and the law that take a freeman out of the bar; the branch is reached by a person who is not a freeman, whom the sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- 39.2 is the only limb with an actor: "we".
-- src:85 | and we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land.
@ref Chapter 39 clause 39.2 (src:85)
GIVEN `the person is a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 39 -- we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` IS
    IF `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` `the person is a freeman` `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers` `it is done by the law of the land` EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         SHANT `set forth against a freeman, or send against him, otherwise than by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 39: the King set forth or sent against a freeman without both the lawful judgment of his peers and the law of the land"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Reading B (fork F39b): "and" taken to mean that either the judgment of peers or the law of the land
-- suffices.  Not the reading taken; it is encoded so that a case can show where the two differ.
-- src:85 | No freeman shall be arrested, or detained in prison, or deprived of his freehold, or outlawed, or banished, or in any way molested;
-- src:85 | and we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land.
@ref Chapter 39 clause 39.1-39.2 (src:85)
GIVEN `the person is a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` IS
    IF `the person is a freeman`
    THEN IF   `it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers`
           OR `it is done by the law of the land`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land".
         THEN `Not barred`
         ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: unless because "unless" names the judgment and the law that take a freeman out of the bar; the branch is reached by a person who is not a freeman, whom the sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- Reading C (fork F39c): the exception belongs to 39.2 alone, because 39.1 ends in a semicolon and
-- 39.2 begins "and we will not ... unless": the passive limb is then without exception.  Not the
-- reading taken.
-- src:85 | No freeman shall be arrested, or detained in prison, or deprived of his freehold, or outlawed, or banished, or in any way molested;
@ref Chapter 39 clause 39.1 (src:85)
GIVEN `the person is a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 39 -- reading C, no exception to the passive limb: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` IS
    IF `the person is a freeman`
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 40 -- right and justice`

-- "To no one": the text does not limit this to freemen (fork F40a); the person is not asked.
-- "We" is the King (fork F1).  What counts as selling, refusing or delaying is taken as a plain fact.
-- src:87 | To no one will we sell, to no one will we refuse or delay, right or justice.
@ref Chapter 40 (src:87)
GIVEN `it is right or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 40 -- right or justice may be sold, refused or delayed` IS
    IF `it is right or justice`
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:87 | To no one will we sell, to no one will we refuse or delay, right or justice.
@ref Chapter 40 (src:87)
GIVEN dealing IS A JusticeDealing
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` IS
    CONSIDER dealing
    WHEN `to sell`   THEN PARTY `the King`
                          SHANT `sell right or justice`
                          HENCE FULFILLED
                          LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 40: the King sold right or justice"
    WHEN `to refuse` THEN PARTY `the King`
                          SHANT `refuse right or justice`
                          HENCE FULFILLED
                          LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 40: the King refused right or justice"
    WHEN `to delay`  THEN PARTY `the King`
                          SHANT `delay right or justice`
                          HENCE FULFILLED
                          LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 40: the King delayed right or justice"
